Z||000000||kinboyatuwo||06-25-2001||03:29 AM||||I need a yelling face and there are none for this<P>Don't know how many of you ride, but i have raced for years (can carry the bike in the fiero!!) and take it pretty seriously.  Well those of you who do it a lot know of trials.<BR>basically obsticles on a bike.<P>was out at night (first mistake) well got up on and to the top of a set of bleacherswent to drop off and miss judged clipped and fell the 5-7', ouch but nothing new except for the multi tool in the rear jersey pocket (second mistake). FUCX that hurt, all brused up and cant walk right, huge dent in my back, let alone ride. With the suspended licence it will suck.<P>well just writing to let off some steam<P>thanks for the room to post<P>injured kin.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/kinboyatuwo/kinboyatuwo.jpg">    <BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."<P>87 Duke, 235,000km||||reg||11
Z||000001||Eric||06-25-2001||10:05 AM||||I went to the local trail this morning.  It's just way too wet to even be out there, but I went anyway.  I got my tires all gunked up with mud, and tried to climb a small hill with roots all over it.  I was able to clear the biggest root with my front tire, but my caked up back tire just spun.  I couldn't get up of my damn clipless pedals, and fell right over on my side.  Fortunatly I wasn't hurt except for a slighly jammed ring finger.  That is the worst trail of all.  It's about time I find someplace new to ride.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Neal||06-25-2001||11:41 AM||||Kinboyatuwo, Is the bike alright  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Any mountain biker knows that people heal and fixing bikes is expensive.<P>Just to add to the stupidity stories.  A guy at work just put a HUGE dent in his spanky new norco torrent frame.  He was jumping on to a picknic table and just bumped the downtube, leaving a nasty looking dent||||reg||1
Z||000003||Standard||06-25-2001||12:47 PM||||I raced yesterday.. and boy was that brutal.  This is my first year racing sport class, and I'm not quite ready for it... thought I was gonna throw up and pass out during the second lap.  I managed to finish, though.  DFL I think, but oh well...<P>'Bout the stupidest thing I've done to one of my bikes was during an urban assault.. jumped and intentionally landed my rear wheel on a cone, the cone crammed my rear derraileur way in toward the spokes.. touched the shifter, derraileur went into the spokes.  Tore the derraileur in half!  Amazingly it barely bent the der. hanger..||||reg||1
Z||000004||baldlobo||06-25-2001||03:27 PM||||you people may know how to fix this on my bike. how do you fix a set of chain links that is stiff; I ask this because my chain skips when it hits this spot in the chain.<P>to add to the stupidity on bikes routein; somehow I managed to f'up(bent it out wards towards the pedel) my front chain guard, and I got pissed off at my front derailer and bent the ****  out of it(that's after it hit my leg). Man, do I miss my old bike it could handle the abuse I put it through(f*ck it got stolen); oh, yeah here is something for canadians; never buy a bike from the bay they are **** . I hope you feel better soon. <p>[This message has been edited by baldlobo (edited 06-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||kinboyatuwo||06-25-2001||07:24 PM||||Update, walking hurts like hell, in bed till 3, brused up nice<BR>guess i banged my knee it is black and blue (didnt notice last night).<BR>Neil:  The bike is okay<BR>its my trials bike and it will hold up to anything, bent the seat rails but not too bad.  Tell your friend the key is to work up to it, find a ramp ant jump up progressively, also leant to land bash ring (have a good one, mine is 5/8" aluminum) and pedal then you pedal up<BR>Standard:<BR>dont worry it only gets better, raced for 6 yrs and the first season is the worst for money (you braek a lot of stuff) and pain, just ride in the gym in the winter.  If you keep it up wait till you make elite, those are races that hurt, two seasons at elite and hurt every monday.<P>BaldLOBO:<BR>hold the chain inbetween your thunbs and forefingers flex the chain both ways putting more and more pressure, see how it moves every once in a while untill it loostens<BR>email with any questions<P><BR>any questions about bikes i can help, i have worked in 3 shops and on some nice bikes<BR>eamil questions, have fixed many a problem over email<P>kin.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/kinboyatuwo/kinboyatuwo.jpg">    <BR>"Friends don't let friends drive four doors."<P>87 Duke, 235,000km||||reg||14
Z||000006||WampusCat||06-25-2001||08:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by baldlobo:<BR>[B]you people may know how to fix this on my bike. how do you fix a set of chain links that is stiff;[B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If the chain isn't doing this because of poor lubrication, then you'll probably need a chain tool to press in the pin and spread the outer plates of the chain a little.<BR>||||reg||1
